1
00:00:00,340 --> 00:00:01,425
[racket swooshes]

2
00:00:01,508 --> 00:00:02,634
[pants]

3
00:00:02,718 --> 00:00:04,177
[boy 1] Taiki just...

4
00:00:04,261 --> 00:00:06,346
[boy 2] Won a match against Haryu.

5
00:00:06,430 --> 00:00:08,682
[panting]

6
00:00:10,100 --> 00:00:12,686
And so, until then, don't lose.

7
00:00:12,769 --> 00:00:13,979
[exclaims softly]

8
00:00:14,938 --> 00:00:16,189
Right!

9
00:00:25,699 --> 00:00:28,827
[Taiki] <i>Was I
holding my own against Haryu?</i>

10
00:00:32,164 --> 00:00:34,166
[opening theme song playing]

11
00:00:35,208 --> 00:00:38,462
BLUE BOX

12
00:01:54,621 --> 00:02:00,919
BLUE BOX

13
00:02:05,048 --> 00:02:07,634
EPISODE 8
SCORE!

14
00:02:07,717 --> 00:02:08,969
[alarm sounds]

15
00:02:12,013 --> 00:02:12,973
[alarm stops]

16
00:02:16,601 --> 00:02:17,561
[sighs]

17
00:02:22,065 --> 00:02:23,775
[birds chirping]

18
00:02:24,901 --> 00:02:25,986
[Chinatsu] Here we go.

19
00:02:26,069 --> 00:02:28,321
[instrumental music playing]

20
00:02:31,950 --> 00:02:33,243
Good morning.

21
00:02:33,326 --> 00:02:34,494
Good morning!

22
00:02:42,377 --> 00:02:43,962
Well, aren't you up early.

23
00:02:44,045 --> 00:02:46,298
Oh, hi, Chinatsu. Good morning

24
00:02:47,132 --> 00:02:49,009
I just couldn't sit still.

25
00:02:49,843 --> 00:02:53,430
{\an8}I kept thinking I'd be super nervous
and tense before the tournament.

26
00:02:53,513 --> 00:02:54,556
{\an8}CALISTHENICS

27
00:02:54,639 --> 00:02:57,559
But now that it's finally today,
I'm psyched.

28
00:02:58,894 --> 00:03:00,020
[exclaims softly]

29
00:03:03,273 --> 00:03:04,816
- Let me join you.
- Huh?

30
00:03:18,788 --> 00:03:20,165
[Taiki] <i>She's so cute.</i>

31
00:03:20,248 --> 00:03:22,334
You're playing doubles today, right?

32
00:03:22,417 --> 00:03:24,544
Um, yes! The singles matches are tomorrow.

33
00:03:28,465 --> 00:03:30,967
How many of you can make it
into nationals, then?

34
00:03:31,051 --> 00:03:34,012
One pair for doubles,
and two players for singles.

35
00:03:34,095 --> 00:03:35,764
Those are pretty tough odds.

36
00:03:35,847 --> 00:03:38,266
Your situation is kinda the same, no?

37
00:03:38,350 --> 00:03:40,477
[Chinatsu] Basketball's
a team sport, though.

38
00:03:40,560 --> 00:03:43,563
Well, I heard that Kagohara
is looking good this year.

39
00:03:43,647 --> 00:03:46,900
Yeah, we're playing them
in the finals, so we have to win.

40
00:03:46,983 --> 00:03:48,777
The finals are tomorrow, right?

41
00:03:49,486 --> 00:03:51,279
[Chinatsu] Yep. Tomorrow.

42
00:03:53,698 --> 00:03:55,242
Already tomorrow.

43
00:04:00,872 --> 00:04:02,916
Um, Chinatsu.

44
00:04:02,999 --> 00:04:06,044
After tomorrow,
could I ask you one question?

45
00:04:07,128 --> 00:04:10,382
<i>I still want to know
why she said she was jealous.</i>

46
00:04:11,800 --> 00:04:14,177
- You don't wanna ask now?
- Nuh-uh.

47
00:04:14,803 --> 00:04:17,931
Okay. Is it all right
if I ask you a question instead?

48
00:04:18,014 --> 00:04:19,015
Huh?

49
00:04:19,099 --> 00:04:21,810
Does badminton club
have any chants you do for each other?

50
00:04:22,602 --> 00:04:24,062
"Score one more"?

51
00:04:24,145 --> 00:04:25,480
"Score one more"?

52
00:04:25,563 --> 00:04:26,648
'Kay, got it.

53
00:04:28,984 --> 00:04:30,735
Then score... one more!

54
00:04:31,319 --> 00:04:32,279
Sure!

55
00:04:33,321 --> 00:04:34,489
[chuckles]

56
00:04:38,493 --> 00:04:41,079
Wow, those exercises refreshed me.

57
00:04:41,162 --> 00:04:44,541
[Taiki] <i>Does she have to keep
making my heart race like that?</i>

58
00:04:46,084 --> 00:04:51,006
SHITAO SPORTS PARK GYMNASIUM

59
00:04:55,093 --> 00:04:57,220
ONE SCORE AT A TIME

60
00:04:57,304 --> 00:04:59,014
- [players playing]
- [all cheering]

61
00:04:59,097 --> 00:05:01,933
DAUNTLESS COURAGE
HEART, SKILL, STRENGTH - PLAY FOR THE WIN!

62
00:05:02,017 --> 00:05:04,019
FLY - EVERY SHOT COUNTS

63
00:05:04,853 --> 00:05:06,271
Dang, it's hot.

64
00:05:07,105 --> 00:05:09,566
It's only mid-June
and it's already scorching.

65
00:05:09,649 --> 00:05:11,234
I dread the rest of the summer.

66
00:05:11,318 --> 00:05:13,028
We can't open the windows, either.

67
00:05:15,030 --> 00:05:16,531
[Taiki] <i>But this atmosphere...</i>

68
00:05:17,866 --> 00:05:21,077
<i>does add to the tournament feel,
so I don't really mind.</i>

69
00:05:24,622 --> 00:05:26,333
KENGO HARYU - TAIKI INOMATA
(EIMEI)

70
00:05:26,416 --> 00:05:28,293
SHOTA HYODO - YUKI TATEYAMA
(SAJIKAWA)

71
00:05:28,376 --> 00:05:30,545
[Haryu] Okay. I should get going.

72
00:05:32,464 --> 00:05:33,548
Where you off to?

73
00:05:33,631 --> 00:05:34,799
{\an8}EIMEI

74
00:05:34,883 --> 00:05:36,551
{\an8}Come with me and see.

75
00:05:40,096 --> 00:05:41,556
This should be a good spot.

76
00:05:42,432 --> 00:05:44,517
[Taiki] <i>We came here to watch a match.</i>

77
00:05:44,601 --> 00:05:45,727
<i>But whose?</i>

78
00:05:46,728 --> 00:05:49,564
[announcer on PA] <i>This is
the call for match number 21.</i>

79
00:05:49,647 --> 00:05:50,607
SAJIKAWA

80
00:05:50,690 --> 00:05:53,526
<i>Hyodo and Tateyama
of Sajikawa High School.</i>

81
00:05:53,610 --> 00:05:55,278
It's the Hyodo-Tateyama pair!

82
00:05:55,361 --> 00:05:56,946
Their aura is on a different level.

83
00:05:57,030 --> 00:05:58,073
They're huge!

84
00:05:58,156 --> 00:05:59,949
[Taiki] <i>So that's Hyodo.</i>

85
00:06:00,033 --> 00:06:02,118
<i>The player Haryu's never beaten.</i>

86
00:06:06,247 --> 00:06:08,958
Oh, hey. If it isn't Haryu.

87
00:06:09,042 --> 00:06:10,835
You come all this way just to lose?

88
00:06:11,711 --> 00:06:13,088
Hey, thanks in advance.

89
00:06:13,171 --> 00:06:15,840
For returning the trophy
that we'll be leaving with today.

90
00:06:16,633 --> 00:06:18,885
I gave it to the organizers, but...

91
00:06:18,968 --> 00:06:20,845
Poor guy, he doesn't get it.

92
00:06:21,596 --> 00:06:23,306
[Tateyama] Hyodo, let's get ready.

93
00:06:24,933 --> 00:06:28,686
Take a good look,
and come up with some counterstrategies.

94
00:06:38,905 --> 00:06:41,282
[Taiki] He's just
oozing confidence, isn't he?

95
00:06:41,366 --> 00:06:43,618
[Haryu] That's 'cause
he's actually that good.

96
00:06:44,744 --> 00:06:48,123
Like if this were baseball,
I could only throw curveballs.

97
00:06:48,206 --> 00:06:52,127
Whereas Hyodo throws curveballs
and killer fastballs.

98
00:06:53,211 --> 00:06:55,547
If we had stats like characters
in video games,

99
00:06:56,214 --> 00:07:00,760
technique, agility, endurance, and speed...

100
00:07:01,469 --> 00:07:04,639
The only player to be maxed out
in all of those stats...

101
00:07:05,473 --> 00:07:06,891
would be him.

102
00:07:14,482 --> 00:07:16,818
Wow, he's in a league of his own.

103
00:07:16,901 --> 00:07:19,404
Seeing that would make anyone wanna quit.

104
00:07:20,321 --> 00:07:22,574
[boy 1] I feel bad
for the kids playing them.

105
00:07:22,657 --> 00:07:25,660
They probably would've gone farther
had they avoided this matchup.

106
00:07:25,743 --> 00:07:28,913
[boy 2] Now it's just a matter
of if they can score any points.

107
00:07:28,997 --> 00:07:31,458
[boy 1] They might be playing
against future Olympians,

108
00:07:31,541 --> 00:07:33,209
so that's a cool memory at least.

109
00:07:35,503 --> 00:07:37,213
Wow, he hit it that way?

110
00:07:37,881 --> 00:07:39,549
I would've done the opposite!

111
00:07:40,216 --> 00:07:42,427
Oh, all that,
and the smash still went too high.

112
00:07:43,219 --> 00:07:46,556
I wonder what would've happened
with a cross-court instead.

113
00:07:46,639 --> 00:07:48,433
Now I wanna try that!

114
00:07:53,521 --> 00:07:56,107
Well, that's easier said than done, Taiki.

115
00:07:56,191 --> 00:07:57,108
[Taiki grunts]

116
00:07:57,775 --> 00:08:00,445
- But now we know what we're up against.
- Huh?

117
00:08:00,528 --> 00:08:02,071
Let's go warm up.

118
00:08:02,155 --> 00:08:03,531
Sounds good.

119
00:08:03,615 --> 00:08:05,617
I think I'll get Nishida to film us.

120
00:08:06,493 --> 00:08:09,704
[Taiki] But he seemed pretty down
after getting eliminated.

121
00:08:11,372 --> 00:08:13,291
[announcer on PA] <i>Match number 28.</i>

122
00:08:19,839 --> 00:08:20,715
Huh?

123
00:08:20,798 --> 00:08:22,467
[snoring]

124
00:08:26,221 --> 00:08:28,223
[Taiki] <i>They dropped their wallet.</i>

125
00:08:28,306 --> 00:08:30,308
<i>Oh. I should tell them.</i>

126
00:08:30,391 --> 00:08:31,976
<i>Even if they are sleeping.</i>

127
00:08:33,520 --> 00:08:34,687
Hello?

128
00:08:41,861 --> 00:08:42,987
Huh?

129
00:08:43,071 --> 00:08:45,490
I think that your wallet
fell out of your pocket.

130
00:08:45,573 --> 00:08:47,158
What? Oh.

131
00:08:49,202 --> 00:08:51,079
I really appreciate it.

132
00:08:51,162 --> 00:08:52,330
[Taiki] No worries.

133
00:08:52,413 --> 00:08:53,748
[Haryu] Taiki, we're up!

134
00:08:53,831 --> 00:08:54,916
Coming!

135
00:08:55,750 --> 00:08:57,252
- See you.
- Mm.

136
00:08:59,963 --> 00:09:01,631
[Yusa] <i>He seemed like a nice guy.</i>

137
00:09:03,299 --> 00:09:04,425
There you are.

138
00:09:04,509 --> 00:09:06,553
Sleeping in random places again, Yusa?

139
00:09:06,636 --> 00:09:07,971
Coach was looking for you.

140
00:09:08,054 --> 00:09:09,180
Huh? Oh.

141
00:09:09,847 --> 00:09:10,848
I'll be right there.

142
00:09:10,932 --> 00:09:11,808
{\an8}SAJIKAWA

143
00:09:13,476 --> 00:09:17,272
[Yusa] <i>But badminton
isn't a sport for nice guys.</i>

144
00:09:18,856 --> 00:09:22,026
SHITAO SPORTS PARK GYMNASIUM

145
00:09:24,529 --> 00:09:25,863
- [boy] Yusa.
- Hm?

146
00:09:25,947 --> 00:09:27,991
What are you doing
with that racket string?

147
00:09:28,074 --> 00:09:30,326
We need to go cheer on Hyodo and Tateyama.

148
00:09:31,619 --> 00:09:32,912
Don't just sit around.

149
00:09:32,996 --> 00:09:36,040
You should really be watching
and learning from your seniors.

150
00:09:37,250 --> 00:09:38,668
[Yusa] <i>Well, that's a given.</i>

151
00:09:38,751 --> 00:09:42,297
They're up against Haryu from Eimei,
so it'll be a fun match to watch.

152
00:09:42,880 --> 00:09:45,800
DAUNTLESS COURAGE

153
00:09:46,593 --> 00:09:48,052
So what did we miss?

154
00:09:48,136 --> 00:09:49,178
Still game one.

155
00:09:49,262 --> 00:09:50,597
Sixteen-nine.

156
00:09:50,680 --> 00:09:52,807
It's looking like it'll be an easy win.

157
00:09:53,641 --> 00:09:55,268
[boy 1] It's too bad for Haryu.

158
00:09:56,019 --> 00:09:59,814
He's talented! But he's never won
an official match against Hyodo.

159
00:10:00,773 --> 00:10:04,652
If he'd been with us, he and Hyodo
could've teamed up and gone to nationals.

160
00:10:06,988 --> 00:10:07,822
[grunts]

161
00:10:07,905 --> 00:10:10,575
[boy 2] And his teammate
is a first year, right?

162
00:10:11,409 --> 00:10:13,578
{\an8}They're down by almost double the points.

163
00:10:14,537 --> 00:10:16,831
I don't think the score
reflects their skill, though.

164
00:10:16,914 --> 00:10:18,041
What?

165
00:10:18,124 --> 00:10:20,585
Their execution
on the court isn't that bad.

166
00:10:20,668 --> 00:10:22,587
They're keeping the rally going.

167
00:10:23,212 --> 00:10:25,590
They just have to find
a way to follow through.

168
00:10:25,673 --> 00:10:27,842
- [grunts]
- [boy] He returned it!

169
00:10:27,925 --> 00:10:31,512
Our team keeps pressing them,
but Haryu isn't backing down!

170
00:10:32,930 --> 00:10:34,474
[inhales] Nice one, Taiki.

171
00:10:34,557 --> 00:10:35,600
Thanks!

172
00:10:36,267 --> 00:10:37,602
You got it!

173
00:10:37,685 --> 00:10:39,103
Nice, Haryu!

174
00:10:40,021 --> 00:10:42,857
[boy] You know, you're right.
That first-year is pretty tough.

175
00:10:42,940 --> 00:10:46,861
His aim may not be perfect,
but his shots always go over the net.

176
00:10:46,944 --> 00:10:48,863
And Haryu's got his back.

177
00:10:48,946 --> 00:10:50,865
[both grunting]

178
00:10:50,948 --> 00:10:53,034
[Nishida] Wow! Nice one, Haryu!

179
00:10:53,951 --> 00:10:55,119
Keep attacking!

180
00:10:55,203 --> 00:10:56,704
[exciting music playing]

181
00:11:14,555 --> 00:11:15,640
[referee] Out!

182
00:11:17,725 --> 00:11:20,728
Aw! That was close,
but they lost the first game.

183
00:11:21,479 --> 00:11:23,147
[Eimei player] You guys got this!

184
00:11:24,607 --> 00:11:25,900
[referee] Change ends.

185
00:11:28,986 --> 00:11:32,031
[Taiki] <i>Damn it.
Just when we were catching up, too.</i>

186
00:11:32,115 --> 00:11:33,991
<i>I need to be landing those shots.</i>

187
00:11:36,744 --> 00:11:38,204
Get outta your head.

188
00:11:38,287 --> 00:11:39,789
The next game, let's win.

189
00:11:40,498 --> 00:11:41,666
Let's win!

190
00:11:44,544 --> 00:11:47,672
{\an8}[Sajikawa player 1] That was close, dude!
His smash was looking good.

191
00:11:47,755 --> 00:11:49,966
[Sajikawa player 2]
If he starts landing shots like that

192
00:11:50,049 --> 00:11:52,260
in the second game,
we might be in trouble.

193
00:11:54,762 --> 00:11:56,472
[footsteps]

194
00:11:59,642 --> 00:12:00,685
[door opens]

195
00:12:01,269 --> 00:12:02,353
Oh. Hello there.

196
00:12:02,437 --> 00:12:04,730
Oh, there you are, Chinatsu! Welcome back.

197
00:12:04,814 --> 00:12:06,649
Congratulations on the finals.

198
00:12:06,732 --> 00:12:09,402
- Fingers are crossed for tomorrow!
- Thank you!

199
00:12:09,485 --> 00:12:11,779
I'm just running to the convenience store.

200
00:12:11,863 --> 00:12:12,697
[Chinatsu] Um...

201
00:12:12,780 --> 00:12:15,283
How did Taiki do today?

202
00:12:18,161 --> 00:12:19,579
[Yukiko] It seems he lost.

203
00:12:23,541 --> 00:12:25,460
[Chinatsu] Tai... ki...

204
00:12:34,260 --> 00:12:35,344
<i>He's asleep.</i>

205
00:12:39,640 --> 00:12:41,642
<i>Reminding him he's a first-year,</i>

206
00:12:42,310 --> 00:12:44,020
<i>or that he still has singles...</i>

207
00:12:45,521 --> 00:12:47,899
<i>probably won't comfort him right now.</i>

208
00:12:47,982 --> 00:12:49,650
MAKE SURE MY SMASHES SCORE!!

209
00:12:49,734 --> 00:12:51,027
<i>It's just that...</i>

210
00:12:52,069 --> 00:12:53,446
[gasps]

211
00:12:54,363 --> 00:12:55,448
[sighs]

212
00:12:57,408 --> 00:12:58,826
How could I forget.

213
00:12:59,494 --> 00:13:01,913
You're not the type
to let this get you down.

214
00:13:16,969 --> 00:13:18,054
[Yukiko] Taiki!

215
00:13:18,638 --> 00:13:19,514
[groans softly]

216
00:13:20,431 --> 00:13:23,809
Sleeping there like that
will affect your performance tomorrow.

217
00:13:23,893 --> 00:13:24,977
[Taiki] You're right.

218
00:13:27,104 --> 00:13:30,107
<i>I think I was dreaming about Chinatsu.</i>

219
00:13:30,691 --> 00:13:31,526
[gasps]

220
00:13:31,609 --> 00:13:33,611
{\an8}MAKE SURE MY SMASHES SCORE!!

221
00:13:33,694 --> 00:13:35,571
{\an8}AND I'LL MAKE SURE I MAKE MY SHOTS!

222
00:13:35,655 --> 00:13:36,948
{\an8}[gasps]

223
00:13:39,909 --> 00:13:42,119
<i>Even her handwriting moves me.</i>

224
00:13:43,120 --> 00:13:46,040
{\an8}SHITAO SPORTS PARK GYMNASIUM

225
00:13:48,918 --> 00:13:50,044
[Haryu] Listen, Taiki.

226
00:13:51,337 --> 00:13:53,381
You'll face me in the finals.

227
00:13:53,464 --> 00:13:56,801
But to get there, you'll have
to take down Hyodo in the semis.

228
00:13:58,511 --> 00:14:00,054
We may've lost in doubles, but you--

229
00:14:00,137 --> 00:14:01,097
I got this.

230
00:14:02,598 --> 00:14:04,433
All I need to do is play my best.

231
00:14:05,142 --> 00:14:06,894
And first is round one.

232
00:14:07,853 --> 00:14:09,605
[Haryu] <i>After losing doubles,</i>

233
00:14:09,689 --> 00:14:12,859
<i>and seeing what he's up against,
I thought he'd be more nervous.</i>

234
00:14:14,235 --> 00:14:15,778
<i>But that's Taiki for you.</i>

235
00:14:22,326 --> 00:14:23,494
[Taiki] <i>I want to win.</i>

236
00:14:24,161 --> 00:14:26,831
<i>Even if I'm up against
one of the best in the country,</i>

237
00:14:27,623 --> 00:14:28,958
<i>I'm giving it my all.</i>

238
00:14:29,041 --> 00:14:31,919
<i>I'll put everything I have
into the match till it's over.</i>

239
00:14:32,795 --> 00:14:36,257
<i>I bet that Chinatsu
is playing the same way, too.</i>

240
00:14:37,675 --> 00:14:40,094
- [shuttlecock thudding]
<i>- That's why.</i>

241
00:14:48,895 --> 00:14:49,854
[referee] In!

242
00:14:51,606 --> 00:14:52,857
Game.

243
00:14:53,691 --> 00:14:56,235
Twenty-one eleven, twenty-one thirteen.

244
00:14:57,945 --> 00:15:00,823
Yusa of Sajikawa High School wins.

245
00:15:07,580 --> 00:15:08,706
Game.

246
00:15:08,789 --> 00:15:11,876
Twenty-one eleven, twenty-one thirteen.

247
00:15:11,959 --> 00:15:14,837
Yusa of Sajikawa High School wins.

248
00:15:15,463 --> 00:15:16,881
[all cheering]

249
00:15:19,216 --> 00:15:20,259
[Taiki] <i>Huh?</i>

250
00:15:21,385 --> 00:15:22,887
<i>It's already over?</i>

251
00:15:28,100 --> 00:15:29,435
Thank you for the match.

252
00:15:34,106 --> 00:15:35,691
And thank you for refereeing.

253
00:15:37,109 --> 00:15:39,195
Winning player, can you please sign here?

254
00:15:40,947 --> 00:15:42,740
[referee] <i>His handwriting sucks!</i>

255
00:15:47,662 --> 00:15:49,914
[Taiki] <i>Oh, right. Since I lost...</i>

256
00:15:50,498 --> 00:15:52,249
{\an8}<i>I have to umpire now.</i>

257
00:15:52,333 --> 00:15:53,417
{\an8}PLAY FOR THE WIN!

258
00:15:56,462 --> 00:15:57,421
[Hina] Wait.

259
00:15:58,547 --> 00:15:59,632
It's over?

260
00:16:00,299 --> 00:16:01,509
[Kyo] Hina.

261
00:16:01,592 --> 00:16:02,927
Hi, Miss Gymnast!

262
00:16:03,010 --> 00:16:04,887
Oh, hi, Kyo. So...

263
00:16:05,429 --> 00:16:07,223
you all still have matches, right?

264
00:16:07,306 --> 00:16:09,308
Like, a round-robin in each division?

265
00:16:09,392 --> 00:16:11,686
Taiki is only just getting warmed up?

266
00:16:11,769 --> 00:16:13,688
No, that's not how it works.

267
00:16:13,771 --> 00:16:15,731
But... Taiki...

268
00:16:16,273 --> 00:16:17,608
He worked so hard.

269
00:16:17,692 --> 00:16:19,944
You're an athlete, too, you get it.

270
00:16:20,695 --> 00:16:22,613
Tournaments end like that.

271
00:16:22,697 --> 00:16:25,658
Being able to play
at the top of your game here is a skill.

272
00:16:26,283 --> 00:16:29,954
You don't win any points
just because you tried, or worked at it.

273
00:16:32,164 --> 00:16:33,249
That's sports.

274
00:16:49,056 --> 00:16:51,225
- [Taiki] At least say something.
- [gasps softly]

275
00:16:52,518 --> 00:16:54,770
Or were you sneaking up on me like always?

276
00:16:57,231 --> 00:17:00,151
As if I would ever be so childish!

277
00:17:00,234 --> 00:17:01,777
You are, all the time.

278
00:17:01,861 --> 00:17:04,071
Should you be speaking to me that way?

279
00:17:04,155 --> 00:17:06,365
When I've brought you something special?

280
00:17:06,449 --> 00:17:07,491
Wait.

281
00:17:07,575 --> 00:17:10,119
Don't tell me you made your special bento.

282
00:17:13,205 --> 00:17:16,876
That was the plan, but I was feeling lazy,
so I brought you snacks.

283
00:17:16,959 --> 00:17:20,129
Oh, thank goodness. No food poisoning.

284
00:17:20,212 --> 00:17:22,506
- What was that, Taiki?
- Uh...

285
00:17:23,340 --> 00:17:25,134
I said I was thankful.

286
00:17:27,887 --> 00:17:30,890
Sorry you came all this way
with these, and for what?

287
00:17:32,141 --> 00:17:33,392
Don't worry about it.

288
00:17:42,234 --> 00:17:44,653
I have to say, sometimes I thought

289
00:17:44,737 --> 00:17:48,240
getting to nationals was gonna be
pretty hard for me at my level.

290
00:17:48,783 --> 00:17:51,118
But I was hoping a big goal would push me.

291
00:17:53,329 --> 00:17:57,166
It made me feel like
I just had to keep going, no matter what.

292
00:17:58,584 --> 00:18:00,920
I do think that I've gotten better.

293
00:18:01,670 --> 00:18:04,465
And then after I won
the game against Haryu,

294
00:18:04,548 --> 00:18:08,177
I actually started to think there
was a chance I could make it to nationals.

295
00:18:09,512 --> 00:18:11,055
At the end of the day,

296
00:18:11,847 --> 00:18:14,809
I suppose I just wasn't
being honest with myself.

297
00:18:18,521 --> 00:18:19,730
This is good.

298
00:18:19,814 --> 00:18:20,856
Real good.

299
00:18:23,484 --> 00:18:25,528
[Hina] <i>You never lose sight of your goals.</i>

300
00:18:26,070 --> 00:18:28,197
<i>And you give it everything you have.</i>

301
00:18:29,115 --> 00:18:31,325
<i>That's what's great about you, Taiki.</i>

302
00:18:31,408 --> 00:18:33,202
[intense music playing]

303
00:18:33,285 --> 00:18:34,203
[grunts]

304
00:18:37,289 --> 00:18:39,375
[cheering]

305
00:18:49,426 --> 00:18:52,054
Another year
of Sajikawa totally dominating.

306
00:18:52,763 --> 00:18:55,474
That Hyodo's a force to be reckoned with.

307
00:18:57,560 --> 00:18:59,311
[organizer] Haryu put up a good fight,

308
00:18:59,395 --> 00:19:02,565
and he's secured a spot in nationals
as a second-year.

309
00:19:02,648 --> 00:19:06,193
Once Hyodo moves on next year,
Haryu's gonna be top dog.

310
00:19:06,819 --> 00:19:10,322
[reporter] Don't forget about Yusa
from Sajikawa. He's one to watch.

311
00:19:11,157 --> 00:19:14,743
He may have lost to Hyodo
in this tournament, but played well.

312
00:19:14,827 --> 00:19:17,037
Can't wait to see where he goes from here.

313
00:19:24,920 --> 00:19:25,921
[gasps]

314
00:19:33,304 --> 00:19:34,263
[referee] Game!

315
00:19:34,847 --> 00:19:38,267
[announcer on PA] <i>The winner
is Hyodo from Sajikawa High School.</i>

316
00:19:38,350 --> 00:19:40,519
[all cheering]

317
00:19:56,869 --> 00:20:00,206
<i>I am going to annihilate him at nationals.</i>

318
00:20:00,831 --> 00:20:01,790
[grunts angrily]

319
00:20:01,874 --> 00:20:04,293
[boy] That face
does not scream "runner-up".

320
00:20:04,376 --> 00:20:06,462
It's gotta be tough losing to Hyodo.

321
00:20:06,545 --> 00:20:07,796
What?

322
00:20:07,880 --> 00:20:09,256
Hey, let's get some food.

323
00:20:09,882 --> 00:20:11,634
Wait, where's Taiki?

324
00:20:12,343 --> 00:20:14,803
I was going to grab a bite
to eat with him.

325
00:20:14,887 --> 00:20:16,180
He went home.

326
00:20:16,263 --> 00:20:18,057
I think he's probably super bummed out.

327
00:20:18,974 --> 00:20:20,100
Yeah, I bet.

328
00:20:22,645 --> 00:20:25,564
SHOPPING DISTRICT

329
00:20:25,648 --> 00:20:27,107
[emotional music playing]

330
00:20:27,191 --> 00:20:29,568
[Taiki] <i>I can't let this
get me down too long.</i>

331
00:20:29,652 --> 00:20:32,404
<i>I have to snap out of it,
and get back to work.</i>

332
00:20:33,072 --> 00:20:35,324
<i>I gotta do something. Practice!</i>

333
00:20:36,700 --> 00:20:38,494
<i>I'll go for it again next year.</i>

334
00:20:39,161 --> 00:20:40,454
INOMATA

335
00:20:40,537 --> 00:20:42,581
<i>I am only a first-year.</i>

336
00:20:43,207 --> 00:20:45,501
<i>I've got two whole chances left.</i>

337
00:20:46,669 --> 00:20:47,586
PREFECTURAL QUALIFIERS

338
00:20:47,670 --> 00:20:50,089
<i>Even if Chinatsu's not here anymore.</i>

339
00:20:53,634 --> 00:20:56,470
[Yukiko] Hey! You are on a roll, Chinatsu!

340
00:20:56,553 --> 00:20:57,596
We're so proud!

341
00:20:58,180 --> 00:21:00,724
I am so, so happy for you!

342
00:21:01,684 --> 00:21:03,602
Count on me to cheer you on.

343
00:21:03,686 --> 00:21:06,021
We've gotta have you strong for nationals!

344
00:21:06,105 --> 00:21:07,564
We'll have a feast tonight.

345
00:21:07,648 --> 00:21:08,983
[Chinatsu] Thank you so much.

346
00:21:10,484 --> 00:21:11,694
[Taiki] <i>That's great.</i>

347
00:21:13,237 --> 00:21:15,656
<i>Chinatsu made it through to nationals.</i>

348
00:21:16,407 --> 00:21:17,408
<i>That's great.</i>

349
00:21:18,200 --> 00:21:19,326
<i>That's great.</i>

350
00:21:20,661 --> 00:21:23,205
<i>Amazing. That's amazing!</i>

351
00:21:23,872 --> 00:21:26,875
<i>She said she would,
and she did it. That's...</i>

352
00:21:28,210 --> 00:21:29,336
<i>really cool.</i>

353
00:21:33,549 --> 00:21:34,633
<i>Even though...</i>

354
00:21:37,094 --> 00:21:38,178
<i>even though...</i>

355
00:21:38,971 --> 00:21:40,848
[runs, pants]

356
00:21:40,931 --> 00:21:42,308
<i>even though...</i>

357
00:21:45,644 --> 00:21:46,895
<i>even though...</i>

358
00:21:56,739 --> 00:21:57,990
<i>I lost.</i>

359
00:22:05,456 --> 00:22:07,458
[closing theme song playing]
